  "title": "Cross-Subject Modeling for Widefield Calcium Imaging via WiCAT",
  "summary": "arXiv AI reports a multi-subject model (WiCAT) that leverages self-supervised pretraining to outperform single-session models and enable zero-shot behavior decoding on unseen subjects, while arXiv Computer Vision highlights its application in widefield calcium imaging. Both studies demonstrate scalability and robustness across neural modalities.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "WiCAT introduces an atlas-grounded tokenization scheme without session-specific components and learns globally shared spatiotemporal representations.",
